{"study_accession":"PRJNA1206180","secondary_study_accession":"SRP555180","title":"Heightened expression of type I interferon signaling genes in CD4+ T cells from acutely HIV-1 infected women is associated with lower viral loads","description":"In this study, we have identified a number of differentially expressed genes in naïve, central memory, and effector memory CD4 T cells of HIV-infected women compared to men, with consistent elevated expression of genes linked to type 1 interferon signaling. Moreover, after controlling for differences in VL and CD4+ T cell count genes within the type I interferon (IFN) signaling pathway were further shown to be more highly expressed in women, whereas, those genes more highly expressed in men showed no such enrichment. A subset of the genes highly expressed in women were further identified, including several involved in type I IFN signaling in response to viral infections (IRF7, DDX58, SAMHD1, OAS2, and TRIM14), that are both more highly expressed in CD4+ T cells from women and negatively correlated with VL, suggesting that they play a role in the comparative control of VL observed in women. Overall design: We have performed bulk RNA-seq experiments comparing gene expression between CD4+ T cells from acutely HIV-1 infected men and women in Zambia, since we observe lower viral load (VL) despite higher CD4+ T cell activation in these women during acute/early infection. We performed analysis on both individual CD4+ T cell subsets (Naive, Central Memory and Effector Memory) as well as combined CD4 T cells) controlling for CD4 T cell counts and viral load.","pubmed":"39902043","geo_series":"","n_samples":24,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"ACUTE_VIRAL_INFECTION","certainty":"confirmed","delta_days":0.0,"delta_bucket":"D0","time_precision":"day","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"A subset of the genes highly expressed in women were further identified, including several involved in type I IFN signaling in response to viral infections (IRF7, DDX58, SAMHD1, OAS2, and TRIM14), that are both more highly expressed in CD4+ T cells from women and negatively correlated with VL, sugge","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN46073330","study_accession":"PRJNA1206180","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"8_305123V03-0_Naive","description":"8_305123V03-0_Naive","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM8710014","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2025-01-09","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","CD4 T cell"],["cell subset","Naive"],["sex","male"],["days post_esitimate_date_of_infection","82"],["log10 viral_load","5.57"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR31885508","experiment_accession":"SRX27243944","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 3000","read_count":7145454,"base_count":721690854,"first_public":"2025-01-09","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 3000 sequencing: GSM8710014: 8_305123V03-0_Naive Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR31885509","experiment_accession":"SRX27243944","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 3000","read_count":16438429,"base_count":1660281329,"first_public":"2025-01-09","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 3000 sequencing: GSM8710014: 8_305123V03-0_Naive Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN46073331","study_accession":"PRJNA1206180","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"6_235072V03-0_Naive","description":"6_235072V03-0_Naive","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM8710013","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2025-01-09","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["cell_type","CD4 T cell"],["cell subset","Naive"],["sex","male"],["days post_esitimate_date_of_infection","87"],["log10 viral_l